A driver sets off, drives at $90$ km/h for $40$ minutes, stops for $25$ minutes, then drives at $72$ km/h for $1$ hour $15$ minutes. What point marks the end of the second driving stage?

questions.solution_text:
$d_{1}=90\times\frac{40}{60}$
$=60\text{ km}$
$d_{2}=72\times1.25$
$=90\text{ km}$
Elapsed time: $40+25+75=140\text{ min}=2\text{ h }20\text{ min}$
Total distance: $60+90=150\text{ km}$
